# WCHNTMaths

Host maths is a `WCHNTMaths` object, same lifecycle as `WCHNTGraphics`.
A free name in an `@` slot is a factory argument. Target passes `wchntMaths`.

Query methods return numbers, so one step can pull as many randoms as it
needs. Void host methods (drawing) stay fluent.

## Schema

```
Trio = Int/a Int/b Int/c
Roll = @WCHNTMaths/maths
```

## Construction

```
[:Roll maths]
```

## Methods

```
Roll::once = {
  r1 = maths.randInt(10).
  r2 = maths.randInt(10).
  r3 = maths.randInt(10).
  [:Trio r1 r2 r3]
}

Roll::wave = { maths.sin(0) }
```

## Target

```
%terminal

%requires
WCHNTMaths::randInt(Int) -> Int
WCHNTMaths::sin(Float) -> Float

%main
public static function main():Void {
    var roll = RollAssemblage.factory(wchntMaths);
    wchntConsole.println(roll.once());
    wchntConsole.println(roll.wave());
}
```
